  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN Trust Fund to End Violence Against Women - UNTFEVAW - 2022-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a multi-partner trust fund managed by UN Women on behalf of the whole of UN. It is the only multilateral trust fund across the UN with a specialised mechanism for call for proposals for capacity building for civil society/women&#x2019;s organisations/women&#x2019;s rights organisations/women-led organisations in their ability to prevent violence against women and girls, improve access to cross sectoral services for survivors of violence, and to support effective implementation of laws and policies of relevance for ending violence against women and children.

The result hierarchy for the new Strategic Plan is:  Impact (tier 1): &#xAB;More women and girls, especially the most marginalised and those experiencing intersecting forms of discrimination, can exercise their human right to live a life free from all forms of violence&#x201D;. Thematic outcome 1 (tier 2): &#x201C;Improved prevention of VAW/G through changes in behaviours, practices and attitudes&#x201D;; Thematic outcome 2 (tier 2): &#x201C;Improved access for women and girls to essential, specialist, safe and adequate multisectoral services&#x201D;; Thematic outcome 3 (tier 2): &#x201C;Increased effectiveness of legislation, policies, national action plans and accountability systems to prevent and end VAW/G&#x201D;.</narrative>
  </description>
